There's another legal avenue, which is, as you say, invoking the Geneva Convention, invoking the Genocide Convention, which Israel is a party to.

15
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:24,320
It has signed that, unlike the International Criminal Court, unlike a lot of other international documents, it has signed the Genocide Convention.

16
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:41,760
Moreover, there's an article in the Genocide Convention that says that any party that's a signer to it can take another party if they even see the prospect that the name of the convention includes the word prevention.

17
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:49,700
That is, you invoke this even to prevent, not just simply to punish genocide, but to prevent it.

18
00:01:50,220 --> 00:02:01,560
So if you see an ongoing genocide or potential genocide taking place, parties which are signatories to this treaty are rather obligated to invoke it.

19
